    "title": "South Dakota football aims to rebound following MVFC opener loss to #1 NDSU on Saturday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anthony Mitchell ,\n2 hours ago VERMILLION, S.D. (KCAU) – The South Dakota Coyotes opened up MVFC play in the loss column following its 51-13 loss to top-ranked North Dakota State on Saturday, totaling just 99 first-half yards.\nIt was a fast start on Saturday that helped propel the Bison to 4-0, scoring five first-half touchdowns to keep the game out of reach early for the Coyotes, who sank to 2-3 on the season.\nSouth Dakota starts the conference slate at 0-1 for the first time in three years. The loss for the ‘Yotes may have been deflating, but has provided the team with a look at where they measure compared to a premier FCS team.\n“A lot of confidence in our building and resilience. Our players and coaches were certainly taking a hard look in the mirror at what we need to do to improve to get on that level to be competitive in a game like that,” South Dakota head coach Travis Johansen said.\n#21 South Dakota will have a chance to return to .500 against Murray State on Dakota Days. Kickoff is scheduled for 2 p.m. in the DakotaDome.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
